      "text": "Given that an integer \\( n \\) when divided by 15 leaves a remainder of 7, we can express this relationship mathematically as:\n\\[ n = 15k + 7 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nWe need to find the remainders when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 and by 5.\n\nFirst, let's determine the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3. We can simplify \\( n \\) modulo 3:\n\\[ n = 15k + 7 \\equiv 0 \\cdot k + 7 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{3} \\]\nSince \\( 7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\), we have:\n\\[ n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\]\nThus, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, let's determine the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5. We can simplify \\( n \\) modulo 5:\n\\[ n = 15k + 7 \\equiv 0 \\cdot k + 7 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSince \\( 7 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\), we have:\n\\[ n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\nThus, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nNow, we need to find the sum of these remainders:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the remainders when the integer \\( n \\) is divided by 3 and by 5 is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
