      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Since when the integer is divided by 15, the remainder is 7, we can express this as:\n\\[ n = 15q + 7 \\]\nwhere \\( q \\) is an integer.\n\nWe need to find the remainders when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 and by 5, and then sum these remainders.\n\nFirst, let's find the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3. We can rewrite \\( n \\) as:\n\\[ n = 15q + 7 \\]\nSince \\( 15q \\) is a multiple of 3, it does not affect the remainder when divided by 3. Therefore, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 is the same as the remainder when 7 is divided by 3. We calculate:\n\\[ 7 \\div 3 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\nSo, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, let's find the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5. We rewrite \\( n \\) as:\n\\[ n = 15q + 7 \\]\nSince \\( 15q \\) is a multiple of 5, it does not affect the remainder when divided by 5. Therefore, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5 is the same as the remainder when 7 is divided by 5. We calculate:\n\\[ 7 \\div 5 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nSo, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nNow, we sum the remainders when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 and by 5:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nThus, the sum of the remainders is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
