      "text": "Given that when an integer \\( a \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7, we can express this relationship mathematically as:\n\\[ a = 15k + 7 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nFirst, we need to find the remainder when \\( a \\) is divided by 3. We do this by considering the expression \\( a = 15k + 7 \\) modulo 3. Since \\( 15k \\) is a multiple of 3, it leaves a remainder of 0 when divided by 3. Therefore, we have:\n\\[ a \\equiv 7 \\pmod{3} \\]\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 7 is divided by 3. We perform the division:\n\\[ 7 \\div 3 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\nSo,\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\]\nThus, the remainder when \\( a \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when \\( a \\) is divided by 5. We do this by considering the expression \\( a = 15k + 7 \\) modulo 5. Since \\( 15k \\) is a multiple of 5, it leaves a remainder of 0 when divided by 5. Therefore, we have:\n\\[ a \\equiv 7 \\pmod{5} \\]\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 7 is divided by 5. We perform the division:\n\\[ 7 \\div 5 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nSo,\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\nThus, the remainder when \\( a \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nThe sum of the remainders when \\( a \\) is divided by 3 and by 5 is:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{3} \\]",
